---
const bandName = 'I Feel More Like I Do Now Than I Ever Have';
const repetitions = Array.from({ length: 400 }, (_, i) => i);

// One background image per section, named for the section rather than
// index-prefixed - order here is what determines each section's index (0 is
// Home, with no nav link - just the top of the site).
const backgroundImages = [
	'/images/backgrounds/Home.jpg',
	'/images/backgrounds/Video.jpg',
	'/images/backgrounds/Events.jpg',
	'/images/backgrounds/Poems.jpg',
	'/images/backgrounds/About.jpg',
];

const loremSnippets = [
	'Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit.',
	'Sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua.',
	'Ut enim ad minim veniam, quis nostrud exercitation ullamco laboris.',
	'Duis aute irure dolor in reprehenderit in voluptate velit esse cillum.',
	'Excepteur sint occaecat cupidatat non proident, sunt in culpa qui officia.',
	'Curabitur pretium tincidunt lacus, et facilisis vel enim nec placerat.',
	'Vestibulum ante ipsum primis in faucibus orci luctus et ultrices posuere.',
	'Praesent commodo cursus magna, vel scelerisque nisl consectetur et.',
	'Nullam quis risus eget urna mollis ornare vel eu leo.',
	'Maecenas sed diam eget risus varius blandit sit amet non magna.',
];
let loremIndex = 0;
function nextLorem() {
	const text = loremSnippets[loremIndex % loremSnippets.length];
	loremIndex += 1;
	return text;
}

const pageOneParagraphs = [
	'Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Ut enim ad minim veniam, quis nostrud exercitation ullamco laboris nisi ut aliquip ex ea commodo consequat.',
	'Duis aute irure dolor in reprehenderit in voluptate velit esse cillum dolore eu fugiat nulla pariatur. Excepteur sint occaecat cupidatat non proident, sunt in culpa qui officia deserunt mollit anim id est laborum.',
	'Curabitur pretium tincidunt lacus, et facilisis vel enim nec placerat. Vestibulum ante ipsum primis in faucibus orci luctus et ultrices posuere cubilia curae; Praesent commodo cursus magna, vel scelerisque nisl consectetur et.',
];

const poemsData = [
	{
		title: 'Consequences (Watering It)',
		body: `I never called it wrong to water it
I called out to the infinite font
The way the breeze hits
The first warm day of the year
Slow, slow
Slow
Trouble not yourself over the cause of my shiver and spit
It troubles you
Didn't water it enough
I couldn't even tell what it was
Or if I even wanted water in the first place
My thirst is infinite
Something inside and ceaselessly dry
You watered it too much
A natural consequence
There are always consequences

I'm stepping on the virus I watered too much [kyle clicky]
I'm not saying I shouldn't have watered it
Given how this breeze hits
On the first warm day of the year
And it all filters back into place
(A little faster now)
(A little faster)
Does it still trouble you?
Is it multiplying in and dividing you?
Water gives it a place to breathe
Did I mention wanting water at all?
Yes infinite font, infinite thirst
Ceaseless and dry
But you watered it too much
There are always consequences
Guess
Thinking slips I spill it onto the time
Birds keep talking in bird talk
How many forms of life before I give out?
Trace the vasculature of our discontents—how long?
Try not to stand them in for something else
Technology spells death in technicolor

I'm losing my grip and unable to refer
Not even sure of what I would do with referring
Throwing words at the screen
Abating at the abattoir
The end of all conceits`,
	},
	{
		title: 'Guess',
		body: `Writing poetry as a means of avoiding the ground
Good luck grounding poetry in the air
Free floating mechanics loose of any contact
Churning through the bloodways
How to jump and touch sky
Way the hunger creeps in
Cutting loose or tying into the universal network of aches, pains, and sunny afternoons with nothing to do

Replacing weed with alcohol: downgrade
Replacing alcohol with religion: category mistake
Replacing the great chasm of loneliness with "somebody please hold me:" equilibrium out loud

My lithium level taken by a waving needle
Vasculature and discontents I wasn't kidding
Enough stability to make you cut your dreams off
Together on the ground again
Leaving ground brings you down harder than would've been

What now? Give up on an airborne existence?
Make a decent living and then what?
Which version of this is it?
I can barely decide what to have for dinner and I am throwing word salad at the only life I will ever have
Wave the needle and ride the anguish over air?
Still wind with bloodflow and concrete?

I guess`,
	},
	{
		title: 'Leaving of the Vine',
		body: `Words lodge in the corners of my skull
Cool evening asks if we're there yet
I'm tilling my dreams again
Fallow for so long
Something provisional seeps in the groundwater
Night air toward quiet
Ambiguity in the realness of when
Night earns a lifetime appointment
Droning on forever in as many years

Yet the day is but a single eye and
I dreamed I was rolling one off into the sunset
Never to be seen again
You old cowboy,
Tumbleweed doesn't smoke to keep you warm
And warmth lingering smokes you
As the tumbleweed rolls over your night
I forget to drink water these days
Desert forgets what forest remembers
Only one meets the night with silence
The other sings over eternal harmony
When will you realize?

You are watched all over by the stars
On this clear and sleepless night

You are watched all over by the stars
On this clear and sleepless night`,
	},
	{
		title: 'Solidarity',
		body: `TBD TBD TBD
TBD TBD TBD
TBD TBD TBD
TBD TBD TBD
TBD TBD TBD
TBD TBD TBD
TBD TBD TBD
TBD TBD TBD
TBD TBD TBD
TBD TBD TBD`,
	},
];

// Content sets, one "page" each - index matches the background image order
// above (Home=0 has no page/link; Video=1, Events=2, Poems=3, About=4).
const pageSets = [
	{ label: 'Video', index: 1, layout: 'video', youtubeId: 'dQw4w9WgXcQ', title: 'Placeholder video - swap for a real one later' },
	{ label: 'Events', index: 2, layout: 'columns-3', items: Array.from({ length: 3 }, () => ({ text: nextLorem() })) },
	{ label: 'Poems', index: 3, layout: 'poems', poems: poemsData },
	{ label: 'About', index: 4, layout: 'tattered-text', paragraphs: pageOneParagraphs },
];
const contentSets = pageSets;

// Nav links embedded in the first 8 (0-7) backdrop-text occurrences, each in
// the gap between two of them (gap i sits between occurrence i and i+1, so
// there are 7 gaps: 0-6). Rules: a link's gap can't be immediately next to
// another link's gap... actually it always isn't - two different gaps are
// never touching since there's always at least one occurrence between them -
// and a link's gap can't be immediately next to whichever occurrence is
// currently the actual-title (its 1-2 bordering gaps are off limits).
const navLinks = pageSets.map((set) => ({ label: set.label, targetIndex: set.index }));
const ACTUAL_TITLE_STATIC_INDEX = 2;
// Static (no-JS) fallback placement - avoids gaps 1 and 2, the two bordering
// ACTUAL_TITLE_STATIC_INDEX. Gap 4 is left empty, same as in the original
// example's spacing.
const STATIC_GAP_ASSIGNMENT: Record<number, (typeof navLinks)[number]> = {
	0: navLinks[0],
	3: navLinks[1],
	5: navLinks[2],
	6: navLinks[3],
};
const NAV_WINDOW_SIZE = 8; // occurrences 0-7, gaps 0-6

// Background image layer (see the parallax script): the whole stacked track
// slides up at this fraction of actual scroll speed.
const IMAGE_PARALLAX_FACTOR = 0.25;

// Content set i peaks (fully opaque) at the same scroll position where
// background image i exactly fills the viewport. Image i sits at i*100vh in
// the untransformed track, and the track has moved up by scrollY *
// IMAGE_PARALLAX_FACTOR px, so image i fully fills the viewport when
// scrollY = i*100vh / IMAGE_PARALLAX_FACTOR - i.e. i * (1 / factor)
// viewport-heights of scroll apart.
const CONTENT_PEAK_SPACING = 1 / IMAGE_PARALLAX_FACTOR;
// One-sided fade duration, in units of one viewport-height of scroll. Equal
// to the full peak spacing, so a set's fade spans the entire gap to each
// neighboring peak: section N is at 0% exactly when N-1 or N+1 is centered,
// and two adjacent sections are each at 50% at the midpoint between them -
// a continuous crossfade, not a fade-out/pause/fade-in.
const CONTENT_FADE_HALF_WIDTH = CONTENT_PEAK_SPACING;
// Highest content-set index (4, since they're 1-4) - used for the min-height
// formula below. Not contentSets.length, since that's now 4 while indices
// run 1-4 rather than 0-3.
const MAX_CONTENT_INDEX = Math.max(...contentSets.map((set) => set.index));

// The two colors used throughout the nav/title system (actual-title,
// inline nav-links, section-nav), named once here instead of as separate
// hex literals in every rule - swapping their roles (as happened once
// already) is then a one-line change, not a hunt across the stylesheet.
const COLOR_PRIMARY = '#fff';
const COLOR_SECONDARY = '#c4ad7a';
---
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<title>IFMLIDNTIEH</title>
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
		<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cormorant&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
		<style define:vars={{ maxContentIndex: MAX_CONTENT_INDEX, contentPeakSpacing: CONTENT_PEAK_SPACING, contentFadeHalfWidth: CONTENT_FADE_HALF_WIDTH, colorPrimary: COLOR_PRIMARY, colorSecondary: COLOR_SECONDARY }}>
			@font-face {
				font-family: 'Shabby';
				src: url('/fonts/Shabby.ttf') format('truetype');
				font-weight: normal;
				font-style: normal;
			}

			html, body {
				margin: 0;
			}

			/* Default for everything except the backdrop band-name text (and
			   the nav styled to match it - see .backdrop-text/.section-nav
			   below, which explicitly set Shabby instead). */
			body {
				font-family: 'Cormorant', serif;
				font-size: 20px;
			}

			body {
				/* Total scroll length is at least enough to reach the last
				   content set's peak and let it fade back out, regardless of
				   how tall the backdrop text happens to wrap to - if the text
				   is taller, the page just grows to fit it instead. */
				min-height: calc((var(--maxContentIndex) * var(--contentPeakSpacing) + var(--contentFadeHalfWidth)) * 100vh);
			}

			.backdrop-text p {
				margin: 0;
				word-break: break-all;
				font-family: 'Shabby', sans-serif;
				font-size: clamp(20px, 6vw, 40px);
				font-weight: bold;
				text-transform: uppercase;
			}

			.backdrop-text p span {
				color: #88a;
				opacity: 0.5;
			}

			/* .nav-gap is also a span under .backdrop-text p - without this,
			   it (and the nav-link button inside it) would inherit the
			   dimming above, washing out the button's own styling. */
			.backdrop-text p span.nav-gap {
				opacity: 1;
			}

			/* The "actual title" - the one real instance of the band name
			   amid all the decorative repetitions. Reads on its own words
			   (not broken mid-word like the rest) and is highlighted white. */
			.backdrop-text p span.actual-title {
				word-break: normal;
				color: var(--colorPrimary);
				opacity: 1;
				text-shadow:
					0 0 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.95),
					0 0 12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9),
					0 0 28px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85),
					0 0 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.75);
			}

			/* Nav links, embedded among the first 8 backdrop-text occurrences
			   (see the frontmatter/script). Styled like .actual-title - same
			   word-break exception, same general glow - but gold instead of
			   white, with a lighter shadow. */
			.backdrop-text .nav-link {
				font: inherit;
				text-transform: inherit;
				word-break: normal;
				color: var(--colorSecondary);
				background: none;
				border: none;
				padding: 0;
				margin: 0 0.3em;
				cursor: pointer;
				transition: color 0.2s ease;
				text-shadow:
					0 0 3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85),
					0 0 9px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.75),
					0 0 18px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65),
					0 0 36px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
			}

			.backdrop-text .nav-link:hover {
				color: var(--colorPrimary);
			}

/* Full section nav, floating independently (not part of the
			   backdrop text flow) along the bottom. Same look as the inline
			   nav-links (font, color, shadow, hover), but its own smaller
			   size - the giant backdrop-text size would be absurd for a
			   small corner UI element. Hidden on Home itself and faded in by
			   the script below once scrolled past it. */
			.section-nav {
				position: fixed;
				bottom: 24px;
				left: 0;
				right: 0;
				z-index: 3;
				display: flex;
				justify-content: center;
				gap: 1.5em;
				opacity: 0;
				pointer-events: none;
				transition: opacity 0.3s ease;
			}

			.section-nav.is-visible {
				opacity: 1;
				pointer-events: auto;
			}

			.section-nav-link {
				font-family: 'Shabby', sans-serif;
				font-weight: bold;
				text-transform: uppercase;
				/* Same basis (vw) as the backdrop text's clamp(20px, 6vw,
				   40px) - between its size and the smaller one this used to
				   be, so it tracks if that one is ever retuned. */
				font-size: clamp(17px, 4vw, 30px);
				word-break: normal;
				color: var(--colorSecondary);
				background: none;
				border: none;
				padding: 0;
				cursor: pointer;
				transition: color 0.2s ease;
				text-shadow:
					0 0 3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85),
					0 0 9px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.75),
					0 0 18px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65),
					0 0 36px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
			}

			.section-nav-link:hover,
			/* Current section indicator - whichever link's section is
			   nearest the current scroll position, ties going to the
			   earlier one (see the script below). Same as hover. */
			.section-nav-link.is-current {
				color: var(--colorPrimary);
			}

			/* No background/border of its own - just sits on whatever's
			   behind it (the page background color, once scrolled past the
			   last background image), so running off the last image reads
			   as "we've reached the footer," not "we ran out of images." */
			.site-footer {
				position: relative;
				z-index: 1;
				padding: 24px 16px;
				color: #ff0;
				font-size: 14px;
				text-align: center;
			}

			/* Layer 2: background images, stacked one per section, pinned to
			   the viewport and slid up by the parallax script at a quarter
			   of actual scroll speed. Sits behind the backdrop text via the
			   negative z-index. */
			.bg-image-layer {
				position: fixed;
				inset: 0;
				overflow: hidden;
				z-index: -1;
				/* Only visible once scrolled past the last background image,
				   where the track runs out and this shows through beneath it. */
				background-color: #2d323b;
			}

			.bg-image-track {
				will-change: transform;
			}

			.bg-image {
				width: 100%;
				height: 100vh;
				background-size: cover;
				background-position: center;
				background-repeat: no-repeat;
			}

			/* Layer 3: content item sets, pinned near the bottom of the
			   viewport. Doesn't physically move - sets crossfade in place as
			   the parallax script updates their opacity based on scroll
			   progress through each section. */
			.content-overlay {
				position: fixed;
				/* vmin, not vh/%, so the margin reads as equal on every side
				   regardless of viewport aspect ratio - except the bottom
				   and right, padded out further to stay clear of the
				   floating Home link in that corner. */
				inset: 5vmin calc(5vmin + 20px) calc(5vmin + 60px) 5vmin;
				z-index: 2;
				pointer-events: none;
			}

			.content-set {
				position: absolute;
				inset: 0;
				opacity: 0;
			}

			.content-items {
				width: 100%;
				height: 100%;
				display: grid;
				gap: 4%;
			}

			.content-set[data-layout='grid-2x2'] .content-items {
				grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
				grid-template-rows: repeat(2, 1fr);
			}

			.content-set[data-layout='single'] .content-items {
				grid-template-columns: 1fr;
				grid-template-rows: 1fr;
			}

			.content-set[data-layout='single'] .content-item {
				width: 70%;
				height: 70%;
				margin: auto;
			}

			.content-set[data-layout='columns-3'] .content-items {
				grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
				grid-template-rows: 1fr;
			}

			.content-set[data-layout='rows-3'] .content-items {
				grid-template-columns: 1fr;
				grid-template-rows: repeat(3, 1fr);
			}

			/* Full-bleed opaque black box with readable body copy, shared by
			   the About page, the Poems page's title rectangles, and its
			   selected-poem display box - rather than one of the big
			   centered-text placeholder cards. The jagged border is a
			   ::before so the SVG filter distorts only the decorative edge,
			   not the actual text. The box itself stays overflow:visible so
			   that ::before's negative inset (it bleeds outside the box)
			   never gets clipped - scrolling (needed when content runs
			   longer than the box) instead happens on a separate inner
			   .tattered-box-scroll wrapper. */
			.tattered-box {
				position: relative;
				width: 100%;
				height: 100%;
				box-sizing: border-box;
				background: #000;
				color: #fff;
				line-height: 1.6;
				text-align: left;
			}

			.tattered-box p {
				margin: 0 0 1em;
			}

			.tattered-box::before {
				content: '';
				position: absolute;
				inset: -6px;
				border: 3px solid #fff;
				filter: url(#tattered-edge);
				pointer-events: none;
			}

			.tattered-box-scroll {
				width: 100%;
				height: 100%;
				overflow-y: auto;
				box-sizing: border-box;
				padding: 6% 7%;
			}

			.tattered-box .poem-body {
				margin: 0;
				white-space: pre-line;
				display: none;
			}

			.tattered-box .poem-body.is-active {
				display: block;
			}

			/* Poems page: a stack of small tattered-box title rectangles on
			   the left (click to select), and one tattered-box on the right
			   showing the selected poem's body text - each box gets its own
			   independent tattered edge via its own ::before, no internal
			   dividers between them, just a gap. */
			.poems-layout {
				display: flex;
				width: 100%;
				height: 100%;
				gap: 4%;
			}

			.poems-titles {
				display: flex;
				flex-direction: column;
				justify-content: space-between;
				gap: 4%;
				width: 30%;
				height: 100%;
			}

			.poem-title-box {
				flex: 0 0 20%;
				display: flex;
				align-items: center;
				justify-content: center;
				text-align: center;
				padding: 6% 7%;
				border: none;
				font: inherit;
				font-size: clamp(14px, 1.8vw, 20px);
				cursor: pointer;
				transition: color 0.2s ease;
			}

			.poem-title-box:hover,
			.poem-title-box.is-selected {
				color: var(--colorSecondary);
			}

			.poems-display {
				flex: 1;
				height: 100%;
			}

			/* Page 2: embedded video, capped to a sane max width and kept at
			   16:9 regardless of the (currently square-ish) content-overlay
			   box it sits in. */
			.content-set[data-layout='video'] .video-box {
				width: 100%;
				height: 100%;
				display: flex;
				align-items: center;
				justify-content: center;
			}

			.content-set[data-layout='video'] iframe {
				width: 100%;
				max-width: 960px;
				aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
				border: none;
			}

			.content-item {
				display: flex;
				align-items: center;
				justify-content: center;
				text-align: center;
				padding: 24px;
				color: #fff;
				font-size: clamp(16px, 2.4vw, 24px);
				background-image: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.75) 0%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45) 60%, transparent 100%);
				/* pointer-events is inherited from .content-set (see below) -
				   not set here, since every set is stacked at the same inset:0
				   position regardless of opacity, and only the currently-
				   visible one should actually be selectable/clickable. */
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<div class="backdrop-text">
			<p>{repetitions.map((i) => (
				<>
					<span class:list={[{ 'actual-title': i === ACTUAL_TITLE_STATIC_INDEX }]} data-index={i} aria-hidden="true">{bandName}</span>
					{i < repetitions.length - 1 && ' '}
					{i < NAV_WINDOW_SIZE - 1 && (
						<span class="nav-gap" data-gap={i}>
							{STATIC_GAP_ASSIGNMENT[i] && (
								<button type="button" class="nav-link" data-target-index={STATIC_GAP_ASSIGNMENT[i].targetIndex}>{STATIC_GAP_ASSIGNMENT[i].label}</button>
							)}
						</span>
					)}
				</>
			))}</p>
		</div>

		<footer class="site-footer">
			<p>
				⚠️ PLACEHOLDER FOOTER ⚠️ — &copy; 2026 I Feel More Like I Do Now Than I Ever Have. All rights reserved (probably). Replace this with real copyright/contact/links later.
			</p>
		</footer>

		<svg width="0" height="0" style="position: absolute;" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
			<filter id="tattered-edge">
				<feTurbulence type="fractalNoise" baseFrequency="0.012 0.06" numOctaves="2" seed="7" result="noise" />
				<feDisplacementMap in="SourceGraphic" in2="noise" scale="10" xChannelSelector="R" yChannelSelector="G" />
			</filter>
		</svg>

		<div class="bg-image-layer" aria-hidden="true">
			<div class="bg-image-track">
				{backgroundImages.map((src) => (
					<div class="bg-image" style={`background-image: url(${src});`} />
				))}
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="content-overlay">
			{contentSets.map((set) => (
				<div class="content-set" data-index={set.index} data-layout={set.layout}>
					{set.layout === 'tattered-text' && (
						<div class="tattered-box">
							<div class="tattered-box-scroll">
								{set.paragraphs.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
							</div>
						</div>
					)}
					{set.layout === 'poems' && (
						<div class="poems-layout">
							<div class="poems-titles">
								{set.poems.map((poem, i) => (
									<button type="button" class:list={['tattered-box', 'poem-title-box', { 'is-selected': i === 0 }]} data-poem-index={i}>
										{poem.title}
									</button>
								))}
							</div>
							<div class="tattered-box poems-display">
								<div class="tattered-box-scroll">
									{set.poems.map((poem, i) => (
										<p class:list={['poem-body', { 'is-active': i === 0 }]} data-poem-index={i}>{poem.body}</p>
									))}
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
					)}
					{set.layout === 'video' && (
						<div class="video-box">
							<iframe
								src={`https://www.youtube.com/embed/${set.youtubeId}`}
								title={set.title}
								allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
								allowfullscreen
							/>
						</div>
					)}
					{set.layout !== 'tattered-text' && set.layout !== 'poems' && set.layout !== 'video' && (
						<div class="content-items">
							{set.items.map((item) => (
								<div class="content-item">{item.text}</div>
							))}
						</div>
					)}
				</div>
			))}
		</div>

		<nav class="section-nav">
			<button type="button" class="section-nav-link" data-target-index="0">Home</button>
			{pageSets.map((set) => (
				<button type="button" class="section-nav-link" data-target-index={set.index}>{set.label}</button>
			))}
		</nav>

		<script>
			// Hard-coded in the markup to index 2 (actual-title) and a fixed
			// gap assignment (nav links), so the page reads and navigates
			// fine with no JS. With JS, both get re-randomized on every load:
			// the actual title moves to one of the first 7 (0-6) occurrences,
			// and the 4 nav links move to 4 of the 7 gaps between the first 8
			// (0-7) occurrences, avoiding whichever gap(s) now border the
			// actual title.
			const ACTUAL_TITLE_RANDOM_RANGE = 7; // 0-6
			const GAP_COUNT = 7; // 0-6, between occurrences 0-7

			function shuffle<T>(items: T[]): T[] {
				const result = items.slice();
				for (let i = result.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {
					const j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1));
					[result[i], result[j]] = [result[j], result[i]];
				}
				return result;
			}

			// Only the band-title occurrences have data-index - the nav-gap
			// spans use data-gap instead, so this doesn't pick those up too.
			const occurrences = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.backdrop-text span[data-index]'));
			const currentActual = occurrences.find((span) => span.classList.contains('actual-title'));
			const newActualIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * ACTUAL_TITLE_RANDOM_RANGE);
			const newActual = occurrences[newActualIndex];

			if (currentActual && newActual && currentActual !== newActual) {
				currentActual.classList.remove('actual-title');
				newActual.classList.add('actual-title');
			}

			const forbiddenGaps = new Set([newActualIndex - 1, newActualIndex].filter((g) => g >= 0 && g < GAP_COUNT));
			const allowedGaps: number[] = [];
			for (let g = 0; g < GAP_COUNT; g++) {
				if (!forbiddenGaps.has(g)) allowedGaps.push(g);
			}

			const navLinkButtons = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.nav-link'));
			navLinkButtons.forEach((button) => button.remove());

			const chosenGaps = shuffle(allowedGaps).slice(0, navLinkButtons.length);
			const shuffledButtons = shuffle(navLinkButtons);

			chosenGaps.forEach((gap, i) => {
				document.querySelector(`.nav-gap[data-gap="${gap}"]`)?.appendChild(shuffledButtons[i]);
			});

			// Poems page: clicking a title rectangle on the left swaps which
			// poem's body text is shown in the single display box on the
			// right - both sides keyed by the same data-poem-index.
			const poemTitleButtons = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.poem-title-box'));
			poemTitleButtons.forEach((button) => {
				button.addEventListener('click', () => {
					const index = button.getAttribute('data-poem-index');
					poemTitleButtons.forEach((b) => b.classList.toggle('is-selected', b === button));
					document.querySelectorAll('.poem-body').forEach((body) => {
						body.classList.toggle('is-active', body.getAttribute('data-poem-index') === index);
					});
				});
			});
		</script>

		<script define:vars={{ imageParallaxFactor: IMAGE_PARALLAX_FACTOR, contentPeakSpacing: CONTENT_PEAK_SPACING, contentFadeHalfWidth: CONTENT_FADE_HALF_WIDTH }}>
			// Parallax layers 2 and 3. One continuous scroll progress value
			// drives both: `progress` is scrollY measured in units of one
			// viewport-height of scroll.
			//
			// Layer 2 (background images) slides at a quarter of actual
			// scroll speed - it's a transform on the whole stacked track,
			// not tied to section boundaries at all.
			//
			// Layer 3 (content sets) doesn't move; each set's opacity is a
			// triangular function of `progress` that peaks at 1 when
			// progress === i * contentPeakSpacing, and reaches 0 exactly
			// contentFadeHalfWidth before/after that - so one set fully
			// fades out before the next fades in, rather than crossfading
			// directly into it.
			const track = document.querySelector('.bg-image-track');
			const contentSetEls = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.content-set'));
			const sectionNav = document.querySelector('.section-nav');
			const sectionNavLinks = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.section-nav-link'));

			function updateParallax() {
				const scrollY = window.scrollY;
				const sectionHeightPx = window.innerHeight;

				if (track) {
					track.style.transform = `translateY(-${scrollY * imageParallaxFactor}px)`;
				}

				const progress = scrollY / sectionHeightPx;
				contentSetEls.forEach((set) => {
					// Content sets are indexed 1-4 (not 0-3), so this reads
					// each set's own data-index rather than its position in
					// contentSetEls.
					const index = Number(set.getAttribute('data-index'));
					const peak = index * contentPeakSpacing;
					const opacity = Math.max(0, 1 - Math.abs(progress - peak) / contentFadeHalfWidth);
					set.style.opacity = String(opacity);
					// Every set is stacked at the same position regardless of
					// opacity, so without this, an invisible set could still
					// steal clicks/selection from the one actually on screen.
					// The video set gets a much higher bar: its embedded
					// player is clickable (and audible) the instant pointer
					// events are on, not just visually present like a div of
					// text is, so it shouldn't arm until mostly faded in.
					const pointerThreshold = set.getAttribute('data-layout') === 'video' ? 0.75 : 0;
					set.style.pointerEvents = opacity > pointerThreshold ? 'auto' : 'none';
				});

				// Hidden until the first content section (index 1, Video) has
				// reached 50% opacity on its way up - visible from there on.
				sectionNav?.classList.toggle('is-visible', progress >= contentPeakSpacing / 2);

				// Current section: whichever peak is nearest, ties going to
				// the earlier (lower-index) section - each section "owns" the
				// scroll range up to and including its own midpoint with the
				// next one, so Math.ceil (not .round) is what gives ties to
				// the lower side.
				const currentIndex = Math.max(0, Math.ceil(progress / contentPeakSpacing - 0.5));
				sectionNavLinks.forEach((link) => {
					const index = Number(link.getAttribute('data-target-index'));
					link.classList.toggle('is-current', index === currentIndex);
				});
			}

			// Table-of-contents buttons jump straight to a set's peak scroll
			// position, recomputed at click time so a resize since load
			// doesn't throw it off.
			document.querySelectorAll('[data-target-index]').forEach((button) => {
				button.addEventListener('click', () => {
					const targetIndex = Number(button.getAttribute('data-target-index'));
					const top = targetIndex * contentPeakSpacing * window.innerHeight;
					window.scrollTo({ top, behavior: 'smooth' });
				});
			});

			updateParallax();
			window.addEventListener('scroll', updateParallax, { passive: true });
			window.addEventListener('resize', updateParallax);
		</script>
	</body>
</html>
